preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "A Dual-Track Framework for GLP-1 Side Effect Estimation: Separating Clinical Evidence from Real-World Patient Reports"
  authors:
    - family-names: Goyal
      given-names: Saurabh
      email: saurabh@magistra.health
      affiliation: "Phlo Systems BV"
  year: 2026
  month: 8
  url: "https://magistra.health/en/methodology"
  abstract: "Patients starting GLP-1 receptor agonist therapy face a persistent information gap: clinical trial side effect frequencies often diverge substantially from the experiences described in patient communities, but existing resources typically report only one or the other. We describe a dual-track estimation framework that collects, extracts, and reports two parallel signals per side effect—a clinical incidence estimate derived exclusively from peer-reviewed clinical trial and regulatory data, and a community reporting frequency (the share of distinct community reports that mention the effect)—without blending them, and without presenting them as comparable quantities. Published estimates are restricted to an eligibility-screened base in which every rate has a citable external origin and each distinct source contributes at most one rate per effect."
